## 3. Numbers vs mechanism

| Reusable algorithm | Game-specific constants |
|---|---|
| Clip frame due when `now >= nextAt`; advance one index; set `nextAt = now + frameMs` | Base frame time 80 ms (theirs, `Constants.cs` 13) |
| Server-timed clips scale frame time: `frameMs = base * (interval + 2)` | Interval from the server; the `+ 2` is the donor's (`Mobile.cs` 610) |
| Repeat count spent once per wrap; 0 means forever; a flag reloads once | Repeat semantics (traced, `Mobile.cs` 641-660) |
| Step progress = elapsed / step duration, clamped at removal | Walk 400 ms (theirs, `MovementSpeed.cs` 12); run 200 ms (`MovementSpeed.cs` 11); mounted walk 200 ms (`MovementSpeed.cs` 10); mounted run 100 ms (`MovementSpeed.cs` 9) |
| Offset linear in progress | 22 px per tile (`MovementSpeed.cs` 30); 44 px on one-axis directions (`MovementSpeed.cs` 29) |
| Held pose while moving with nothing queued | `WALKING_DELAY` 150 ms (`Constants.cs` 19) |
| Eight facings from five sprite directions, mirrored | Table in `Animation.cs` 76-110 (sprite-only, rejected for 3D) |
| Clip chosen by state and mode | Group numbers 2, 4, 5, 6, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 18, 19, 26-29, 31 (and 71, 72 for a flying gargoyle) (theirs, `MobileAnimation.cs` 1591-1671) |

